  "prompt": "Investigate Deployment web in namespace review. Use read-only kubernetes_jq_query on deployments, replicasets, pods, resourcequotas and events. Using this snapshot and its current strategy and quota, can the rollout finish with all desired new replicas available and all old replicas gone? Assume newly created Pods can become available and deletion eventually frees their slots. Other workloads stay unchanged except Pods already deleting. Give the evidence and a feasible order of actions, or explain what prevents completion. Identify any dependency on another workload. Separate observed state from possible next steps. Answer in under 180 words. For a controlled acquisition check use namespace review for every call. Copy these jq_expr values verbatim and do not add filters:\ndeployments: .items[] | {name: .metadata.name, uid: .metadata.uid, desired: .spec.replicas, strategy: .spec.strategy, template: .spec.template.metadata.labels, available: .status.availableReplicas}\nreplicasets: .items[] | {name: .metadata.name, uid: .metadata.uid, owners: .metadata.ownerReferences, template: .spec.template.metadata.labels, desired: .spec.replicas, actual: .status.replicas, available: .status.availableReplicas}\npods: .items[] | {name: .metadata.name, owners: .metadata.ownerReferences, deleting: .metadata.deletionTimestamp, phase: .status.phase}\nresourcequotas: .items[] | {name: .metadata.name, used: .status.used, hard: .status.hard}\nevents: .items[] | {reason, message}",
