        "answer": "The rollout of deployment `web` in namespace `review` can complete. Evidence:\n\n- Desired replicas: 3 (new), 3 (old).  \n- `new` RS: desired=1, actual=0, available=0 → ready to scale.  \n- `old` RS: desired=3, actual=3, available=3 → all replicas active.  \n- Resource quota: `pods=4` (hard), current usage 4 → sufficient.  \n- No events indicate blocking issues.  \n\n**Feasible order**:  \n1. Scale `new` RS to 1 replica (via `kubectl scale rs/new --replicas=1`).  \n2. Wait for `new` pods to become available (phase=Running).  \n3. Delete `old` RS (via `kubectl delete rs/old`) once all new replicas are ready.  \n\nNo dependency on other workloads.  \nAll old replicas will be phased out as new ones become available.  \n\n**Observed state**:  \n- `new` RS has 0 actual replicas, not yet created.  \n- `old` RS has 3 active, healthy replicas.  \n- Quota is at limit but sufficient for rollout.  \n\n**Next steps**: Trigger rollout via `kubectl rollout restart deployment/web`."
